{"reason": "The current pipeline relies on a single 80/20 train/validation split and basic single-column group statistics, limiting feature expressiveness and generalization. Physiological health indicators contain multi-factor interaction patterns across demographic sub-groups that basic features fail to capture. Upgrading to a 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation scheme with multi-group aggregations and out-of-fold threshold optimization maximizes data utilization and test set robustness.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "CHANGES: Category: Feature Engineering. What: Extend feature engineering with higher-order physiological interaction terms (metabolic recovery index, hydration density per BMI unit, cardiac-metabolic stress product) and multi-group demographic aggregations (grouping numeric features by composite keys such as gender x physical_activity_level and diet_type x smoking_alcohol). Why: Physiological health markers depend heavily on compound demographic context (e.g. resting heart rate and step counts have different normal ranges when stratified jointly by gender and activity level). How: Expand `build_physiological_features` to compute composite continuous interaction ratios and construct group z-score metrics across composite categorical groupings. Interface constraints: Maintain function signature `build_physiological_features(df)` and return a pandas DataFrame compatible with model training.", "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: Category: Training Strategy & Ensembling. What: Replace single 80/20 split with 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation to generate out-of-fold (OOF) probability predictions and average test predictions across folds. Why: Single 80/20 split underuses 20% of training data and suffers from split variance, whereas 5-Fold OOF predictions enable leak-free optimization of ensemble weights and class thresholds across the full training dataset. How: Train LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and TabularResNet on each fold, store OOF probability predictions, optimize ensemble weights and class decision thresholds via Nelder-Mead on full OOF predictions, and average test predictions across all 5 folds. Interface constraints: Maintain target encoding mapping {'at-risk': 0, 'fit': 1, 'unhealthy': 2}, output submission to `./submission/submission.csv`, and print `Final Validation Score: {score}` computed using balanced accuracy."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
