  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "CHANGES: Add non-linear clinical deviation features and group aggregations in data_processing_and_feature_engineering. WHAT: Compute ideal sleep deficit `abs(sleep_duration - 7.5)`, resting heart rate anomaly `abs(heart_rate - 70.0)`, BMR metabolic proxy interactions, and missing interaction terms, alongside multi-group aggregations computed strictly on train data. WHY: Health classification relies heavily on non-linear physiological departures from healthy normal ranges, which simple linear ratios fail to capture. HOW: Modify `engineer_features()` to create deviation metrics and add new group stats aggregated on `['smoking_alcohol', 'stress_level']` fitted strictly on `df_train`. Interface constraints: Preserve `X_train_feat`, `X_val_feat`, `X_test_feat`, and column data types.",
    "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: Apply balanced sample weighting to XGBoost and optimize model blend weights dynamically in training_evaluation. WHAT: Compute balanced class sample weights for XGBoost fitting and upgrade ensemble post-processing to optimize model weights jointly with class thresholds. WHY: XGBoost was previously unweighted, giving uncalibrated probabilities on imbalanced classes, while fixed blending weights (0.35, 0.30, 0.25, 0.10) sub-optimally combine model outputs. HOW: Pass `sample_weight=compute_sample_weight('balanced', y_train)` to `xgb_model.fit()`, and use `scipy.optimize.minimize` with Nelder-Mead on validation balanced accuracy to solve for optimal model blend coefficients and class multipliers simultaneously. Interface constraints: Maintain final output path `./submission/submission.csv` and keep `Final Validation Score` print statement."
  }
}"}

