    "model_design": "Tier 3 Paradigm Shift: Expand the candidate model family by combining LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and ExtraTreesClassifier designed for multi-class classification. Integrate CatBoost with native categorical feature support alongside gradient boosting models to maximize ensemble diversity across tree structures. Ensure all models expose compatible fit and predict_proba interfaces for fold-based training. Maintain function signature get_gbdt_models(seed=42) and ensure returning a dictionary of configured model estimators.",
    "training_evaluation": "Tier 3 Paradigm Shift: Implement full 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation across the entire training dataset to train all base models and collect out-of-fold (OOF) class probability predictions. Fit a calibrated Multinomial Logistic Regression meta-model on the concatenated OOF probability matrix to learn optimal dynamic blending weights and decision thresholds for Balanced Accuracy. Compute final test predictions by averaging test probabilities across all 5 folds and transforming them via the trained meta-learner. Preserve target mapping, output submission to ./submission/submission.csv, and print print(f'Final Validation Score: {score}') using 5-fold overall OOF balanced accuracy."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "The baseline solution relies on a single 80/20 validation split and lacks rich multi-categorical interaction features. Single split optimization on Nelder-Mead threshold weights suffers from variance and leaves 20% of training data unused during final inference. Implementing 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation with Out-Of-Fold (OOF) probability aggregation alongside targeted categorical interaction features will maximize data utilization and produce reliable ensemble weights across the entire dataset.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "CHANGES: Feature Engineering Expansion. WHAT: Add explicit categorical combination features (e.g., gender_activity, diet_stress, smoking_stress), numerical interaction ratios (e.g., heart_rate * stress_level_ord, water_intake per 1k steps), and out-of-fold target encodings. WHY: Patient health risk relies heavily on non-linear joint interactions across discrete clinical profiles and vital signs. HOW: Update engineer_features to build combined categorical strings, compute targeted physiological product ratios, and fit K-Fold out-of-fold target encodings within each CV split to maintain strict data isolation. Maintain existing target column and raw feature names for complete compatibility.", "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation Ensembling & OOF Threshold Optimization. WHAT: Replace single train/val split with 5-Fold Stratified K-Fold CV for LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and PyTorch ResNet, generating full out-of-fold validation predictions and fold-averaged test predictions. WHY: Ensembling across 5 folds stabilizes predictions, prevents overfitting of post-processing probability multipliers, and utilizes 100% of training data. HOW: Implement StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42), train each model family across all folds, collect OOF probability matrices, and optimize Nelder-Mead ensemble weights and class calibration multipliers on the full OOF array before evaluating final balanced accuracy."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The baseline solution relies on a single 80/20 validation split and lacks rich multi-categorical interaction features. Single split optimization on Nelder-Mead threshold weights suffers from variance and leaves 20% of training data unused during final inference. Implementing 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation with Out-Of-Fold (OOF) probability aggregation alongside targeted categorical interaction features will maximize data utilization and produce reliable ensemble weights across the entire dataset.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
