  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "CHANGES: Feature Engineering Expansion. WHAT: Add explicit categorical combination features (e.g., gender_activity, diet_stress, smoking_stress), numerical interaction ratios (e.g., heart_rate * stress_level_ord, water_intake per 1k steps), and out-of-fold target encodings. WHY: Patient health risk relies heavily on non-linear joint interactions across discrete clinical profiles and vital signs. HOW: Update engineer_features to build combined categorical strings, compute targeted physiological product ratios, and fit K-Fold out-of-fold target encodings within each CV split to maintain strict data isolation. Maintain existing target column and raw feature names for complete compatibility.",
    "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation Ensembling & OOF Threshold Optimization. WHAT: Replace single train/val split with 5-Fold Stratified K-Fold CV for LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and PyTorch ResNet, generating full out-of-fold validation predictions and fold-averaged test predictions. WHY: Ensembling across 5 folds stabilizes predictions, prevents overfitting of post-processing probability multipliers, and utilizes 100% of training data. HOW: Implement StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42), train each model family across all folds, collect OOF probability matrices, and optimize Nelder-Mead ensemble weights and class calibration multipliers on the full OOF array before evaluating final balanced accuracy."
  }
}"}

