{"reason": "The baseline model plateaued at 0.9504 using a single 80/20 split and basic single-column group features, leaving 20% of training data unutilized during model fitting. Biometric indicators (e.g., heart rate, calorie expenditure) have clinically distinct normal ranges depending on composite lifestyle context (e.g., gender combined with physical activity level). Implementing composite multi-group demographic aggregations paired with 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation ensembling across LightGBM, CatBoost, and XGBoost will capture nuanced subgroup interactions and improve test set generalization.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "CHANGES: Category: Feature Engineering & Subgroup Aggregations. What: Construct composite demographic grouping keys (e.g., gender x physical_activity_level, diet_type x smoking_alcohol) and compute subgroup statistics (mean, std, min, max, z-scores) for core biometric metrics (bmi, heart_rate, step_count, calorie_expenditure), alongside advanced clinical interaction ratios (metabolic BMR residual, hydration adequacy index, cardiovascular stress load). Why: Physiological risk signals are context-dependent and best measured as deviations from demographic cohort norms. How: Expand `build_physiological_features` to compute composite keys, derive group aggregations on the training split, map them to train/val/test without leakage, and return augmented feature DataFrames while preserving existing column names and interface constraints.", "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: Category: Training Strategy & Ensembling. What: Upgrade model training to a 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation scheme for LightGBM, CatBoost, and XGBoost, generating full out-of-fold (OOF) probability predictions and averaging test predictions across all 5 folds. Why: 5-Fold CV trains models on 100% of available data across folds, drastically reduces prediction variance on test set, and provides complete OOF probability distributions for reliable threshold optimization. How: Implement `StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5)`, fit GBDT models per fold with early stopping on validation folds, accumulate full OOF predictions, optimize class decision thresholds via Nelder-Mead on full OOF predictions to maximize balanced accuracy, and write test predictions to `./submission/submission.csv` while printing `Final Validation Score: {score}`."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
