  }
}"}

{"reason": "The validation score has plateaued at 0.9501 because linear probability blending and simple weight multipliers fail to capture complex non-linear decision boundary interactions between multi-class predictions. To break this plateau, we apply a Tier 3 Systemic Paradigm Shift: replacing simple linear ensembling with a 2-stage Stacking Meta-Learner pipeline that processes Out-Of-Fold (OOF) prediction matrices from a widened ensemble of diverse estimators (LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, ExtraTrees, and Tabular ResNet) coupled with class-balanced meta-learning.", "module": ["model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"model_design": "CHANGES: [Category: Model Architecture & Stacking] 1) Expand the candidate model pool by introducing ExtraTreesClassifier with balanced class weighting alongside LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and Tabular ResNet to enhance model diversity across feature space splits. 2) Design a second-stage Stacking Meta-Learner (LogisticRegression with class_weight='balanced') that takes concatenated out-of-fold class probability predictions from all primary models as input features to learn non-linear probability recalibrations. 3) Keep loss functions and variable interfaces compatible across all component boundaries.", "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: [Category: Training Strategy & Post-Processing] 1) Implement 5-fold Stratified K-Fold cross-validation to construct a leak-free OOF prediction matrix across all base models for both validation and test sets. 2) Fit the stage-2 Stacking Meta-Learner on the OOF probability matrix to generate Meta-OOF and Meta-Test probabilities. 3) Apply Nelder-Mead threshold and weight optimization directly on the Meta-Learner output probabilities to maximize balanced accuracy macro-recall. 4) Generate predictions on test set via the stacked pipeline and output to ./submission/submission.csv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The validation score has plateaued at 0.9501 because linear probability blending and simple weight multipliers fail to capture complex non-linear decision boundary interactions between multi-class predictions. To break this plateau, we apply a Tier 3 Systemic Paradigm Shift: replacing simple linear ensembling with a 2-stage Stacking Meta-Learner pipeline that processes Out-Of-Fold (OOF) prediction matrices from a widened ensemble of diverse estimators (LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, ExtraTrees, and Tabular ResNet) coupled with class-balanced meta-learning.",
