}"}

{"reason": "The solution plateaued at 0.9504 due to reliance on hardcoded manual blending weights (0.35/0.30/0.25/0.10) on a single split, which fails to learn complex non-linear combinations or class-conditional prediction strengths across diverse base models. To break this plateau, a Tier 3 Systemic Paradigm Shift is required to transition from manual blending to a 2-stage Stacking Meta-Learner paired with 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation. Training a meta-classifier on Out-Of-Fold (OOF) probability predictions allows the pipeline to learn optimal multi-model representations and maximize Balanced Accuracy.", "module": ["model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"model_design": "CHANGES: Category: Stacking Meta-Learner Architecture (Tier 3 Paradigm Shift). What: Replace hardcoded linear weight blending with a 2-stage Stacking Architecture utilizing a regularized Logistic Regression meta-classifier fitted on out-of-fold probability predictions from LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and ExtraTrees. Why: Manual probability weighting cannot dynamically learn class-specific confidence trade-offs between gradient boosters, whereas a trained meta-learner learns optimal multi-model synergy. How: Define a Stage-2 meta-model `LogisticRegression(C=0.5, max_iter=1000, multi_class='multinomial')` that consumes concatenated OOF probability matrices (or logit transformations) from Stage-1 models to generate unified meta-probabilities.", "training_evaluation": "CHANGES: Category: Out-Of-Fold Stacking & Threshold Optimization Strategy. What: Execute a 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation scheme to generate leak-free OOF predictions for all Stage-1 models, train the Stage-2 meta-learner on full train OOF probabilities, and apply post-hoc Nelder-Mead threshold optimization on Stage-2 OOF predictions. Why: Generating OOF predictions across 5 folds utilizes 100% of training data, prevents meta-overfitting, and aligns probability thresholds strictly with the target Balanced Accuracy metric. How: Run `StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5)`, train Stage-1 models with early stopping per fold, accumulate test set predicted probabilities averaged across folds, train Stage-2 meta-model on train OOF, run Nelder-Mead on Stage-2 OOF probabilities to find class scaling weights that maximize `balanced_accuracy_score(y_train, meta_oof_preds)`, apply optimal weights to test meta-probabilities, save predictions to `./submission/submission.csv`, and print `Final Validation Score: {score}`."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The solution plateaued at 0.9504 due to reliance on hardcoded manual blending weights (0.35/0.30/0.25/0.10) on a single split, which fails to learn complex non-linear combinations or class-conditional prediction strengths across diverse base models. To break this plateau, a Tier 3 Systemic Paradigm Shift is required to transition from manual blending to a 2-stage Stacking Meta-Learner paired with 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation. Training a meta-classifier on Out-Of-Fold (OOF) probability predictions allows the pipeline to learn optimal multi-model representations and maximize Balanced Accuracy.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
